{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>(בשעריך) תאכלנו — You shall eat it.</b> [This means] one who is fit to eat it. <b>שנה בשנה — Year by year,</b> not that it is forbidden to eat it after its year, for it is likened to the second tithe, of which it is said (Deuteronomy 14): ״ואכלת לפני ה' אלהיך מעשר דגנך״ and so forth, ובכורות בקרך — and the firstborn of your cattle, and that is not disqualified from one year to the next; rather, it is a commandment to eat it within its year. <b>אתה וביתך — You and your household,</b> the household of the priest."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:32.270125214Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}